      "text": "**The internationalist thesis**: Coubertin believed that international competition under sportsmanlike rules would build mutual respect between nations. \"The important thing in the Olympic Games is not winning but taking part; the essential thing in life is not conquering but fighting well.\" This Coubertin quote is widely cited but the historical attribution and precise wording is contested -- some version of it appears in his writings."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-MODERN-OLYMPICS.md#012",
      "path": [
        "04-MODERN-OLYMPICS.md"
      ],
