        "title": "The Modern Olympics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Coubertin's blind spots**: He was explicitly opposed to women's Olympic competition. He considered women's sport aesthetically unpleasant and contrary to the nature of the Games. Women's events were included over his objection, beginning with tennis and golf in 1900. His class assumptions were embedded in the amateurism rules he designed."
    },
